  "id": "Enfield-26_03060_FUL",
  "cil_liability": false,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "In failing to provide evidence that prerequisite notice was served to the owner of the property at least 21 days prior to the submission of the application, and in light of correspondence from the owner of the property discrediting this, the Local Planning Authority cannot be satisfied that the application accords with the provisions of Section 65 of the Town & Country Planning Act 1990.",
    "The change of use into a house of multiple occupation (Use Class C4) results in an excessive number and clustering of conversions along this stretch of Baker Street, unduly at odds with the predominant pattern of single family dwellinghouses along the road. The proposed development would thereby be contrary to Policies; CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD 5 and DMD 37 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014) as well as the NPPF (2026).",
    "The proposed development, by reason of its inadequate floor to ceiling heights at first floor level would give rise to the provision of substandard accommodation for occupiers of Bedrooms 3 and 4 incapable of meeting the reasonable needs of occupiers of these bedrooms. Furthermore, Bedroom 5, by reason of the fact that it is served only by a single high level roof light which is orientated to face towards the sky, would provide prospective occupants with inadequate outlook to the detriment of their overall living conditions. The proposed development would thereby be contrary to Policies; D3 and D6 of the London Plan, CP 4 and CP 30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD 5, DMD 6, and DMD 8 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), in addition to the high-quality design aspirations set out within the NPPF (2026)."
  ]
